WEBVTT

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.240
- I won't be long.
- Got it.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.850
Fernando...

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.750
Jean!

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.830
Are you back from military service?

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.820
Why are you here?!

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.540
How dare you show yourself to my sister!

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.200
You live all nice and comfortable,
instead of making the Padania pay!

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:26.470
Well?! Say something!

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.550
I'm sorry.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.900
That shirt...

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.870
Are you part of the left-wing movement?!

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:50.210
I wouldn't if I were you. Getting
caught up in politics is dangerous.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:53.780
I have to make them pay!

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.110
I have to avenge my sister!

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.250
Why... Why?

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:11.690
I was proud of you.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:17.690
I couldn't wait to be brothers
after you and my sister got engaged!

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.780
What is it, Brother?

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:27.610
I ran into Fernando.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:31.780
Fernando? He came to visit her grave too?

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.780
He was acting strangely.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:37.090
Tail him when he leaves.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.750
Okay.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:08.350
Sofia... These past two years,
I've killed 56 Padania members.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:14.350
I will continue to fight, until
they're gone from this earth.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.690
"The Light of Venice,
The Darkness of the Heart"

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:50.790
Damn!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:03.470
Hey, it's me. I'm heading
to the apartment now.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:06.130
Yeah. I'll need a gun.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:51.990
Don't try anything funny!
Don't throw your life away!

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.320
You're a cop?! Dammit!

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:12.340
The bastard was planning
to attack that apartment.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:13.280
Whose is it?

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:19.120
I asked around. Supposedly,
a man from Venice moved in recently.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.120
The Venice Faction?

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:28.420
Hasn't Venice been sending
terrorists into Rome lately?

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:32.030
Fernando appears to be part
of the left-wing movement.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:35.100
He probably heard about
the apartment from a comrade.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:39.430
I'd force him to talk, if he
weren't an acquaintance of yours.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.530
What do we do, Jean?

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.350
If a Padania member lives here,
we take care of him and go.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:51.340
Got it. I'll get ready.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.090
Hey, Angelica.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.890
So, what happens to Fernando?

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:03.260
We give him to the police and have
him cool off for a week or two.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:06.030
It must be frustrating.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:08.530
I know exactly how he feels.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:10.860
Yeah, I guess so.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:23.480
Ready, Angelica?

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.470
Yes, Marco-san!

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:34.580
- Who is it?
- The police! I'd like to talk!

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:47.590
No, you don't!

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.620
Jean!

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.530
Giuse, make him talk.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:33.240
Got it.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.030
Rico.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.950
What are you doing there?

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.120
Umm... My hands...

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.110
We have work to do.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.870
What's wrong?

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.270
You can't stand up?

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:02.940
J-Jean-san!

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.600
I've no need for someone who's useless.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:50.150
You have everything you need, Rico?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.810
Yes, Jean-san.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:58.450
We'll take the car to Rome.
We'll be in Venice in the afternoon.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:01.520
- Umm, Jean-san.
- What is it?

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:03.510
Where did you get that cut?

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:07.500
Don't worry about it. It's nothing.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:09.160
Yes, sir.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:18.470
There's a large wealth gap between
this country's north and south.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:24.480
As such, the rich northerners want
to turn Italy into a federal union.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:29.080
These radical nationalists are
known as the Five Republics Faction,

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:33.420
because of its original advocacy
for breaking Italy into five pieces.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.060
Milan is in the north.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:41.730
Rome is in the middle,
and Naples is in the south.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:46.140
Add in Sicily and Sardinia
and that makes five.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.870
Then what's the Venice Faction?

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.880
The Milan Faction wanted to
separate the entire northern area.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:57.380
The Venice Faction only wanted
to liberate the Veneto province.

00:11:57.380 --> 00:12:01.920
And that caused
factional strife between them.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:04.910
Almost sounds straight
out of the Renaissance Era.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:13.430
He's a Padania politician.

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:14.960
Padania?

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.600
The Milan Faction once called
itself the Padania Republic Faction

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.940
and declared its independence.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.930
So now it's another name
for the Five Republics Faction.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:31.680
Then there are still
many enemies around?

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:34.650
We gave them a harsh
lesson in Milan a while back,

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:37.310
but there are still many others out there.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.290
"Venice, Veneto Province"

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:47.120
Whoops. Pardon me.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:49.290
That's all right.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:52.730
- Are you Jean-san from Rome?
- Yes.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:55.130
I'm Altmeyer of the Venice Branch.

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:56.790
Thanks for coming.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:06.810
Your name... Is it German?

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:08.280
Yes.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:13.850
Makes it hard for me with the
Venice Faction always sniffing around.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:17.020
So, what brings you here suddenly?

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:21.680
We caught word of some Padania
operatives here. We need a guide.

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.570
We branch offices focus
on information-gathering.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.560
Please don't go causing trouble.

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:37.500
We can handle trouble ourselves.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:51.890
There are a lot more
patrol boats nowadays.

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:53.220
Yes.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:55.460
Is there a lot of terrorism here?

00:14:55.460 --> 00:15:00.930
No. The Padania doesn't
attack sightseeing locations.

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:03.600
It's for foreigners' peace of mind,

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.930
because Europe has a strong
image of being politically unstable.

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:12.140
They're policemen on military service.

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:17.010
Yep. They wear uniforms
but are barely trained.

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:21.120
Parades are about all they're good for.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.350
Say, Jean-san.
Let's hurry and get to work.

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:28.350
Don't rush. We wait until night.

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:39.700
Do you know the man
living at this address?

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:43.040
Yes. He's a local Mafia boss.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.480
He's sending terrorists into Rome.

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:48.710
That's news to me.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:54.720
It's no surprise that local Mafia
are with the Venice Faction, though.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.350
What's the plan?

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:59.190
We're going to go and either
capture him or kill him.

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:03.450
Huh?! Just you and this little girl?

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:12.170
That's crazy! His bodyguards
are former San Marco marines!

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:18.660
You know she's no ordinary
child. She's a useful tool.

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:41.490
What is it?

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:45.200
H-Hello there!

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:19.700
All done, Jean-san!

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:39.010
H-Hey!

00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:45.130
We gotta go before more show up!

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.120
Jean-san. Look...

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:55.760
This PC is still logged in.

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:59.610
We can use it to learn
about the organization.

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:02.040
- Tomorrow will be fun.
- Yes, sir.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:05.150
Hey... You...

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:10.140
E-Even after this,
you're still not satisfied?

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:14.280
Of course not.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:22.220
"San Giorgio Maggiore"

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:42.150
Rico! Stop that boat! Kill if you have to!

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:43.810
Yes, sir!

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:07.300
Rico!

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:09.970
She's been hit!

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.260
Rico! Are you all right?!

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:49.470
So pretty...

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:13.230
Do you enjoy looking
out at the sea that much?

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:18.400
Yes. It's very pretty. It's breathtaking.

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:32.650
It makes me sad. Especially at sunset.

00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:38.560
Nothing. Go on and play now.

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:41.220
- I'll be relaxing here.
- Yes, sir!

00:22:34.050 --> 00:22:49.060
A doll without a heart,
born from warm hands

00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:58.340
I neither smile nor talk

00:22:58.340 --> 00:23:06.510
I want you to hear
about these feelings someday,

00:23:06.510 --> 00:23:14.560
though they can't be put into words

00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:22.830
I'll summon all my strength

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:46.350
to know what it means to live
